<title>JAPAN: Namibia's Nujoma asks Japan for drought aid.</title>
<headline>Namibia's Nujoma asks Japan for drought aid.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Namibian President Sam Nujoma on Tuesday asked for Japan's help to combat a severe drought in his country, a Japanese Foreign Ministry official said.</p>
<p>Nujoma, who is on a five-day visit to Japan, requested the aid in a meeting with Prime Minister Ryutaro Hashimoto, the official told reporters.</p>
<p>Nujoma told Hashimoto the drought was the worst in 100 years and had damaged livestock, Namibia's main export product, dealing a serious blow to its economic development.</p>
<p>The official, who asked not to be identified, said Nujoma also asked for Tokyo's support in lifting an international ban on ivory exports, at least from Namibia and other southern African nations.</p>
</text>
